        <NDF-RT:MeSH_CUI>M0022928</NDF-RT:MeSH_CUI>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_DUI>D014901</NDF-RT:MeSH_DUI>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>A mosquito-borne viral illness caused by the WEST NILE VIRUS, a FLAVIVIRUS and endemic to regions of Africa, Asia, and Europe. Common clinical features include HEADACHE; FEVER; maculopapular rash; gastrointestinal symptoms; and lymphadenopathy. MENINGITIS; ENCEPHALITIS; and MYELITIS may also occur. The disease may occasionally be fatal or leave survivors with residual neurologic deficits. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1996, Ch26, p13; Lancet 1998 Sep 5;352(9130):767-71)</NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>West Nile Fever</NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>
