        <NDF-RT:MeSH_DUI>D006582</NDF-RT:MeSH_DUI>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>A chlorinated bisphenol antiseptic with a bacteriostatic action against Gram-positive organisms, but much less effective against Gram-negative organisms. It is mainly used in soaps and creams and is an ingredient of various preparations used for skin disorders. (From Martindale, The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p797)</NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>Hexachlorophene</NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>
