        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A compound, RkE(=O)lNHOH, derived from an oxoacid RkE(=O)l(OH) (l =/= 0) by replacing -OH with -NHOH, and derivatives thereof. Specific examples of hydroxamic acids are preferably named as N-hydroxy amides.</obo:IAO_0000115>
