        <NDF-RT:UMLS_CUI>C0019345</NDF-RT:UMLS_CUI>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>Herpes simplex, caused by type 1 virus, primarily spread by oral secretions and usually occurring as a concomitant of fever. It may also develop in the absence of fever or prior illness. It commonly involves the facial region, especially the lips and the nares. (Dorland, 27th ed.)</NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>
