        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>Cardiomyopathies</NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>A group of diseases in which the dominant feature is the involvement of the CARDIAC MUSCLE itself. Cardiomyopathies are classified according to their predominant pathophysiological features (DILATED CARDIOMYOPATHY; HYPERTROPHIC CARDIOMYOPATHY; RESTRICTIVE CARDIOMYOPATHY) or their etiological/pathological factors (CARDIOMYOPATHY, ALCOHOLIC; ENDOCARDIAL FIBROELASTOSIS).</NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>
