    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://evs.nci.nih.gov/ftp1/NDF-RT/NDF-RT.owl#N0000170352">
        <NDF-RT:UMLS_CUI>C0042287</NDF-RT:UMLS_CUI>
        <NDF-RT:Display_Name>Valinomycin</NDF-RT:Display_Name>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://evs.nci.nih.gov/ftp1/NDF-RT/NDF-RT.owl"/>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_CUI>M0022498</NDF-RT:MeSH_CUI>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>A cyclododecadepsipeptide ionophore antibiotic produced by Streptomyces fulvissimus and related to the enniatins. It is composed of 3 moles each of L-valine, D-alpha-hydroxyisovaleric acid, D-valine, and L-lactic acid linked alternately to form a 36-membered ring. (From Merck Index, 11th ed) Valinomycin is a potassium selective ionophore and is commonly used as a tool in biochemical studies.</NDF-RT:MeSH_Definition>
        <NDF-RT:code>C7759071830917</NDF-RT:code>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_DUI>D014634</NDF-RT:MeSH_DUI>
        <NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>Valinomycin</NDF-RT:MeSH_Name>
        <NDF-RT:RxNorm_CUI>11116</NDF-RT:RxNorm_CUI>
